<section class="content-section"><div class="shell content-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">What this route addresses</div><h2>Start with the operating issue.</h2><p>Technology is selected only after the problem, authority, information boundary and desired outcome are understood.</p></div><div class="indexed-list"><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">01</span><div><h3>Clarify the trigger</h3><p>Understand what is driving the review, timing and business consequence.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">02</span><div><h3>Resolve scope and authority</h3><p>Separate client-declared context from the requirements that can only be established through governed assessment.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">03</span><div><h3>Prepare the evidence position</h3><p>Identify what information exists, where it sits and what will require controlled intake later.</p></div></div><div class="indexed-item"><span class="index">04</span><div><h3>Plan the next governed step</h3><p>Move from readiness into scoped consulting work only after security and human review.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
